<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Severians (Balkan)</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 681 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Slavic tribe in north-eastern Bulgaria whom the Bulgars under Asparuh placed to guard the eastern passes of the Balkan Mountains.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known mainly from Byzantine chronicles, the Severi were a Slavic tribe that settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> in the 7th century, in the area between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta and the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived as a tribal people under their own chiefs. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> arrived under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asparuh-of-bulgaria">Asparuh</a> in 680–681, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theophanes-the-confessor">Theophanes</a> records that the Severi were moved to guard the passes towards <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seven-slavic-tribes">Seven Slavic Tribes</a> held other borders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>, keeping their own leaders for some time; in the 760s the Byzantine emperor Constantine V captured Slavun, chief of the Severi. They then merged into the Bulgarian population.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 600 CE – 681 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.64%;width:1.61%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 681 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Slavun</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Severi, Sever tribe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=640&amp;focus=severians-balkan" aria-label="Severians (Balkan) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5295 674 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Severians (Balkan) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5653 895h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5615 930h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5615 930h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Bulgaria. <a href="/atlas?year=640&amp;focus=severians-balkan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
